---
import { sitePath } from "../../utils/paths";
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Research" active="Research"><section class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Research</p><h1>Biological systems,<br/><span>one molecule at a time.</span></h1><p class="lead">Molecular simulation is the common thread in my work: understanding membrane behavior, exploring molecular interactions, and developing computational workflows.</p></section><section class="container research-list"><a class="research-row" href={sitePath("/research/electroporation/")}><span class="row-number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Membrane biophysics</p><h2>Electroporation &<br/>molecular transport</h2><p>How can electric pulses influence the formation and lifetime of membrane pores?</p><span class="text-link">Explore the research →</span></div><img src={sitePath("/images/electroporation-figure-4.webp")} alt="Membrane pore snapshots at successive times" loading="lazy"/></a><a class="research-row" href={sitePath("/research/semdock/")}><span class="row-number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Protein–small-molecule interactions</p><h2>Virtual screening &<br/>reproducible workflows</h2><p>How can raw chemical collections become a practical starting point for molecular docking?</p><span class="text-link">Explore the research →</span></div><img src={sitePath("/images/semdock-abstract.webp")} alt="Graphical overview of semdock" loading="lazy"/></a><a class="research-row" href={sitePath("/research/molecular-transport/")}><span class="row-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Membrane biophysics · First-author research</p><h2>From pore formation<br/>to molecular transport</h2><p>Connecting atomistic simulations with quantitative diffusion modeling.</p><span class="text-link">Explore the research →</span></div><img src={sitePath("/images/transport-figure-2.webp")} alt="Molecular snapshots of electropore formation" loading="lazy"/></a></section>
<section class="container academic-section" aria-labelledby="current-research-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Current research</p><h2 id="current-research-heading">Autophagy & molecular interactions.</h2>
  <p class="academic-intro">At Islamic University, I lead the computational biology arm of a HEAT project investigating drug discovery through the regulation of autophagy in cancer. I use virtual screening against p62 and molecular dynamics to investigate small-molecule–protein interactions, alongside GUV preparation for experimental membrane studies.</p>
  <a class="text-link" href={sitePath("/about/#experience")}>Research experience →</a>
</section>
<section class="container academic-section" aria-labelledby="methods-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Methods & expertise</p><h2 id="methods-heading">Across scales and approaches.</h2>
  <div class="academic-grid">
    <article class="academic-card"><h3>Molecular dynamics</h3><p>All-atom and coarse-grained simulations of membranes, electroporation, and molecular interactions using GROMACS and NAMD; trajectory analysis with MDAnalysis, VMD, and PyMOL.</p></article>
    <article class="academic-card"><h3>Screening & interaction modeling</h3><p>Protein structure prediction, protein–protein and protein–ligand modeling, and high-throughput virtual screening using AlphaFold, ClusPro, AutoDock Vina, RDKit, OpenBabel, Meeko, and gmxMMPBSA.</p></article>
    <article class="academic-card"><h3>Quantitative transport</h3><p>PDE modeling and numerical simulations in MATLAB and COMSOL Multiphysics connect pore geometry with molecular transport.</p></article>
    <article class="academic-card"><h3>Experimental biophysics</h3><p>Giant unilamellar vesicle preparation, fluorescence microscopy, and confocal laser microscopy complement computational studies of membranes.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="container related-research" aria-labelledby="related-research-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Related publications</p>
  <h2 id="related-research-title">More on membrane transport.</h2>
  <div class="related-research-list">
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">Applied Biological Research · 2025</p>
      <h3>Molecular transport by varying the size of nanopore in the membrane of GUV using simulation</h3>
      <p>COMSOL modeling of the influence of nanopore diameter and molecular size on transport through giant unilamellar vesicle membranes.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.48165/abr.2025.27.01.22" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the paper ↗</a>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">Bangladesh Journal of Physics · 2024</p>
      <h3>Transport through asymmetric multipores in giant unilamellar vesicles</h3>
      <p>Finite-element simulations of nanopore-mediated transport, extending the continuum-modeling theme of my membrane research.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.3329/bjphy.v31i2.79519" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the paper ↗</a>
    </article>
  </div>
  <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/publications/')}>View complete publication list →</a>
</section>

</Base>
